			"notes": "Patch release on top of 0.1.0-alpha. Same requirements: Minecraft 26.3, Fabric Loader 0.19.5+, Fabric API, Java 25.\n\nChanges:\n\n* Fullpack reload is about 20 times faster with large packs. Pack resources were listed by walking the whole pack tree for every request; a reload with a few hundred MB of converted Bedrock addons went from 40 s to 2 s, and world start got the same speedup.\n* Removed Fullpack content no longer vanishes. Blocks and items of a deleted or disabled pack keep their id as missing content: no use, no placement, a \"Missing\" name, their own creative tab, placed blocks keep their state and block entity data. This also holds across restarts through `koperlib/registry_manifest.json`. Entities are not covered yet. See \"Reload or restart\" in the docs.\n* Khysics: foundation for fast flight, with body frames and an opt in dimension flight policy.\n\nJars are the same three as before:\n\n* `koperlib-core` is required by the other two.\n* `koperlib-fullpack-apis`: Fullpacks, KUI, Kodel models and KFX effects.\n* `koperlib-khysics`: Khysics physics and the Elpe engine.\n\nNatives are included for Linux x86_64 and Windows x86_64."
		},
